course: dictionary
lesson: 16149
title: Words with two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To pick the right one, read the words around the word, which are its context. «Ben talked about himself for an hour and never let anyone else speak. What a windbag!» The clues are talked for an hour and never let anyone else speak, so a windbag here is a person who talks too much.
explain: Windbag also has an older meaning. «Grandpa squeezed the bagpipes, and air filled the windbag with a loud hum.» Here there is no person at all. The windbag is the bag of a bagpipe that holds the air. Ask yourself: does a person fit here, or an object? That question often settles it.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have probably chosen well. If it does not, try the other meaning.
fact: Windbag is an informal word, so you hear it in chatty talk more than in formal writing.
fact: «Windbag» means a person who talks too much, usually about boring or unimportant things, or who boasts endlessly.
fact: «Windbag» can also mean the bag of a bagpipe that holds the air. This is an old meaning.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, Toad could be called a windbag because he boasts and talks about himself without stopping.
fact: Politicians are sometimes mocked as windbags, which means people tease them for talking a lot without saying much that is useful.
exercise: «Ben talked about himself for an hour and never let anyone else speak. What a windbag!» What is a windbag in this sentence? | *A person who talks too much | A strong wind that blows leaves about | A quiet friend who listens well | A bag that holds air for bagpipes
exercise: «Grandpa squeezed the bagpipes, and air filled the windbag with a loud hum.» What is the windbag in this sentence? | A cloth bag for shopping | A person who boasts | *The bag of a bagpipe that holds the air | A kind of storm cloud
exercise: Why might a writer call Toad a windbag in The Wind in the Willows? | *Because he boasts and talks about himself without stopping | Because he carries a big bag of food | Because he likes to fly kites | Because he is very quiet and shy
test: «Jack talks about football all day and never asks what anyone else thinks.» What does windbag suggest about Jack? | *He talks too much and does not let others join in | He is lost and needs help | He is a good listener | He plays music in a band
test: Which sentence uses windbag in its old sense, about bagpipes? | «My windbag friend tells the longest stories.» | «Sam is such a windbag that nobody wants to sit near him.» | «The windbag of the storm blew the washing off the line.» | *«The piper pumped air into the windbag until the pipes began to sound.»
exam: «Politicians are sometimes mocked as windbags.» Why might people call politicians windbags? | *Because people feel they talk a lot without saying much useful | Because they play bagpipes at every meeting | Because they live in very windy places | Because they never speak in public at all
